<title>POLAND: Polish KPW clears Tonsil new share issue.</title>
<headline>Polish KPW clears Tonsil new share issue.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) cleared Polish loudspeaker systems maker Tonsil SA's new issue of 590,000 shares, earmarked mostly for its creditors, KPW said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The company earlier said 530,000 of the new shares would go to its creditors -- 450,000 to the treasury in exchange for a 7.8 million zloty debt and 80,000 to businessman Krzysztof Niezgoda for a 1.45 million zloty debt.</p>
<p>The remaining 60,000 shares, at an issue price of 17.29 zlotys, could be purchased by Japan's Tohoku Pioneer Electronic Corporation to allow it to it keep its current 10 percent stake in Tonsil.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
